  "notes": "Stripe colors vary by aircraft, all in the same layout: Island green #078A6E (drawn here, the default: the commonest with Sea), Sea blue #0858B8 (CFG/sea), Passion red #EC4226 (CFG/passion), Sunshine yellow-orange #F0A63C (CFG/sunshine), Beach sand #BAA472 (CFG/beach); the four are copies of this file with their stripe color, and change with it. Green re-checked 2026-11-22 on D-ANCK (2026-07-07, ground, sunlit: midtone #198576) and D-ANMY (2025-06-06: #14745E); #078A6E kept. The stripe positions are measured on an A320neo (D-ANCW): a colored nose cap to x 0.04, then 11 stripes about 0.042 wide every 0.0857, the last running out to the tail cone; longer types (A321neo, A330-900) show the same rhythm. The tail-cone color band and the fin's trailing band are one stripe. Older aircraft not yet repainted fly the 2004-2022 white scheme with a yellow fin and Condor's former logo; 80% of the fleet was planned to be striped by 2024. Heights near the window line are placed relative to the windows (about y 0.13), as the photos show them, rather than measured absolutely. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on D-ANCW (right side, 2026-03-05): 'condor' runs x 0.155-0.274, its lowercase 0.65 of the d's ascender; 'est. 1956' about 0.12 of the fin's chord.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximation (white with a yellow fin, the old scheme). The stripes replaced the yellow-tailed Condor scheme and the brief Thomas Cook-era heart scheme from April 2022."
}
